.TH "CRYPTO" "1" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBcrypto\fR \- Tool to encrypt or decrypt standard input using OpenSSL (RSA seal/open or AES\-256\-CBC)
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
crypto rsa\-enc <pubkey\.pem>   < plaintext > container\.txt
crypto rsa\-dec <privkey\.pem>  < container\.txt > plaintext

crypto aes\-keygen <keyfile>
crypto aes\-enc <keyfile>      < plaintext > container\.txt
crypto aes\-dec <keyfile>      < container\.txt > plaintext
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBcrypto\fR is a small CLI tool that reads all data from standard input and writes the result to standard output\.
.P
It supports:
.IP "\[ci]" 4
\fBRSA hybrid encryption\fR via OpenSSL \fBEVP_Seal*\fR / \fBEVP_Open*\fR (\fBrsa\-enc\fR / \fBrsa\-dec\fR)
.IP "\[ci]" 4
\fBAES\-256\-CBC\fR symmetric encryption via OpenSSL \fBEVP_Encrypt*\fR / \fBEVP_Decrypt*\fR (\fBaes\-enc\fR / \fBaes\-dec\fR)
.IP "" 0
.P
Every mode requires a key file argument\. Keys are never embedded in the output container\. The tool is designed for piping and scripting \(em it prints no interactive prompts and no labels on output\.
.SH "MODES"
.SS "rsa\-enc <pubkey\.pem>"
Reads plaintext bytes from \fBstdin\fR, encrypts using RSA hybrid "seal" (RSA\-encrypted session key + AES\-256\-CBC data encryption), and writes a single\-line container to \fBstdout\fR\.
.P
The recipient's \fBpublic key\fR PEM file is required\. The corresponding private key never leaves the recipient's side and is never transmitted\.
.SS "rsa\-dec <privkey\.pem>"
Reads a single\-line RSA container from \fBstdin\fR, decrypts it using the given \fBprivate key\fR PEM file, and writes plaintext bytes to \fBstdout\fR\.
.SS "aes\-keygen keyfile"
Generates 48 cryptographically random bytes (32\-byte AES\-256 key + 16\-byte IV) and writes them to \fBkeyfile\fR\. Use this to create a key file before running \fBaes\-enc\fR or \fBaes\-dec\fR\. Prints a confirmation message to \fBstderr\fR\.
.SS "aes\-enc keyfile"
Reads plaintext bytes from \fBstdin\fR, encrypts using AES\-256\-CBC with the key and IV loaded from \fBkeyfile\fR, and writes a single\-line container to \fBstdout\fR\.
.P
The key is \fBnot\fR included in the container output\. Both the sender and receiver must possess the same key file\.
.SS "aes\-dec keyfile"
Reads a single\-line AES container from \fBstdin\fR, loads the key from \fBkeyfile\fR, and writes plaintext bytes to \fBstdout\fR\.
.SH "KEY FILE FORMAT"
.SS "RSA keys"
Standard PEM format, compatible with OpenSSL:
.IP "" 4
.nf
# Generate a 2048\-bit RSA key pair
openssl genpkey \-algorithm RSA \-pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 \-out private\.pem
openssl pkey \-in private\.pem \-pubout \-out public\.pem
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SS "AES key file"
A binary file of exactly \fB48 bytes\fR: the first 32 bytes are the AES\-256 key, the next 16 bytes are the AES\-CBC IV\. Use \fBaes\-keygen\fR to create one\.
.SH "CONTAINER FORMAT"
All \fB*\-enc\fR modes output a \fBsingle line\fR to \fBstdout\fR:
.P
\fBRSA container\fR (\fBrsa\-enc\fR):
.IP "" 4
.nf
b64(ciphertext)\.b64(encryptedSessionKey)\.b64(IV)
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
\fBAES container\fR (\fBaes\-enc\fR):
.IP "" 4
.nf
b64(ciphertext)\.b64(IV)
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Each \fBb64(\|\.\|\.\|\.)\fR is Base64\-encoded without newlines\. The AES key is \fBnot\fR present in the container\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.SS "Generate an RSA key pair and perform a round\-trip"
.nf
openssl genpkey \-algorithm RSA \-pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 \-out private\.pem
openssl pkey \-in private\.pem \-pubout \-out public\.pem

printf "hello\en" | \./crypto rsa\-enc public\.pem | \./crypto rsa\-dec private\.pem
.fi
.SS "Generate an AES key file and perform a round\-trip"
.nf
\&\./crypto aes\-keygen my\.key
printf "test" | \./crypto aes\-enc my\.key | \./crypto aes\-dec my\.key
.fi
.SS "Encrypt a file and decrypt it"
.nf
\&\./crypto aes\-keygen my\.key
\&\./crypto aes\-enc my\.key < input\.bin > out\.container
\&\./crypto aes\-dec my\.key < out\.container > input\.bin\.recovered
.fi
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IP "\[ci]" 4
\fB0\fR on success
.IP "\[ci]" 4
\fB1\fR on errors (missing/invalid key file, invalid container, crypto failure, I/O failure)
.IP "\[ci]" 4
\fB2\fR on usage error (wrong number of arguments or unknown mode)
.IP "" 0
.SH "SECURITY NOTES"
.IP "\[ci]" 4
RSA containers do \fBnot\fR embed any key material\. Confidentiality relies entirely on keeping the private key file secret\.
.IP "\[ci]" 4
AES containers do \fBnot\fR embed the key\. The key file must be kept secret and shared securely out\-of\-band with the decrypting party\.
.IP "\[ci]" 4
Input is limited to 256 MiB to prevent unbounded memory growth\.
.IP "\[ci]" 4
Key material is wiped from memory using \fBOPENSSL_cleanse\fR before being freed\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBopenssl(1)\fR, \fBopenssl\-genpkey(1)\fR, \fBopenssl\-pkey(1)\fR, OpenSSL EVP documentation
